<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3061" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăpollĭnāris</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		Apollo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>belonging</i> or <i>sacred to Apollo</i>, <i>of Apollo.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laurea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 2, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Apollinarem (aedem),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					3, 63, 7</span></i>
			 Weissenb.—Hence, Ludi Apollinares, <i>the games celebrated in honor of Apollo</i>, <i>annually</i>, <i>on the 5th of July</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 25,
			12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">27, 23</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Att. 2, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Phil. 10, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 35,
				10, 36, § 19 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăpol-lĭnāris</span></b> ,
			is, f. (sc. herba), <i>the
				herb commonly called hyoscyamus</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 26,
				14, 87, § 140</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A species of solanum</i>,
				<i><span class="en">App. Herb. 22</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
